  bx('ye', "<b>CIC conflict:</b> handout figure calls the 1793 CIC 'ex-officio'; text and teacher say <b>extra-ordinary</b>. Use text + teacher. <b>Code:</b> civil personal law = community custom (State can reform: Sati Abolition Act 1829, Removal of Religious Disabilities Act 1850, Hindu Widow Remarriage Act 1856, Hindu Succession Act, Triple Talaq, UCC, abolition of untouchability COI 1950); civil non-personal (property, contracts) = State law; criminal always non-personal (State vs accused)."),

  sec("CHARTER ACT 1813: WESTERNISATION BEGINS", 'b'),
  t("<b>Context</b>", "<b>Narrative:</b> <b>Adam Smith's Wealth of Nations (1776)</b> free market (laissez faire): monopoly under attack since 1776; <b>Liberals, Utilitarians, Evangelists</b>: British manufacturers would industrialise India (technology, FDI) = <b>White Man's Burden (WMB)</b>; heavy lobbying by manufacturers + non-EIC traders ('Recall: interlopers', Ch 10)", "<b>National interest:</b> <b>Industrial Revolution 1750-1850</b>: till IR Britain wanted <b>finished goods (FG)</b> from India, so big MNC EIC + monopoly; once IR matured wanted <b>raw material (RM)</b> + India as export market for machine-made FG: trader monopoly no longer in interest", "<b>Westernisation push:</b> 'Great Ancient India = myth'; three arms: <b>polity and administration, economy (machines, factories), society (education, customs, religion, reforms)</b>", w=26),
