  t("<b>@GG (8)</b>", "<b>1 Landmark:</b> GG(Bengal)-in-Council became <b>GG(India)-in-Council</b>: 'Governor' now rules all Br India (Bengal, Bombay, Madras) = true <b>PM of Br India</b>; need of uniform law (one country, one law, one executive; GST, Napoleonic Code 1804); board 'implementation of law'", "<b>2</b> GG(India) <b>executive + legislative head</b>: laws for all Br India, equal for Indians + Britishers", "<b>3</b> <b>Legislative powers of Bombay + Madras Governors taken away</b> (restored by <b>Indian Councils Act 1861</b>, Ch 25)", "<b>4</b> <b>Centralisation peaks 1833; decentralisation begins 1861, peaks 1935</b>", "<b>5</b> <b>One Law Member (Thomas Macaulay)</b> added to draft uniform laws: grain of <b>separation of executive and legislative</b> at council level (GG still heads both); start of separate legislature", "<b>6</b> <b>Law Commission 1834</b> under Macaulay: codification; done <b>1837</b>; full implementation post-1857: <b>CPC 1859, IPC 1860, CrPC 1861</b> (board also lists <b>Indian Evidence Act</b>); <b>2024</b> replaced by <b>BNS, BNSS, Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam</b>", "<b>7</b> <b>Racial equality:</b> 'No person to be deprived of chance to enter EIC service on grounds of religion, race, birth or colour'; <b>Uncovenanted Civil Services (UCS, ~Group B)</b> + subordinate judicial posts below district judge (e.g. <b>Munsifs</b>) opened to Indians to <b>cut cost</b> (teacher: 'not imp')", "<b>8</b> Charter renewed <b>20 years</b>", w=30),
