  bx('pk', "<b>Teacher's four verdicts:</b> <b>no Qs in Mains</b>, few rare Qs in Prelims, troubles aspirants in every book, best version in this handout. Subject = history of <b>Public Administration (PubAd)</b> in British India. <b>ORG (the State) = its three machines. 'WORK = RULE'</b> over <b>T (territory)</b> and <b>Ppl (people)</b>: Company State took the territory; this chapter = how it handled the people (L, E, J shorthand Ch 8, 10). Administration = how the State implements policies, laws, schemes on the ground; Company State <b>1765-1858</b> (Charter 1833 ended commerce); EIC had to decide how much Indian machinery to keep or replace."),
