  sec("JUDICIAL SYSTEM IN RYOTWARI AREAS", 'b'),
  t("<b>Madras 1814, Bombay 1819</b>", "Bengal model (separated functions) suits <b>zamindari</b> (few big landowners, few disputes, distant court workable); <b>Ryotwari = very many small landowners</b>, many disputes, district courts physically distant (board 'WHR number of landowners is LESS')", "<b>Madras 1814:</b> Bengal system replaced on <b>Munro's advice</b>; separation ended; <b>European DC + subordinates given judicial powers</b> for ground-level justice (less paperwork, faster); <b>greater Indianisation of lower judiciary</b> (juniors include Indians; board scale 300, 200, 100)", "<b>Downside: concentration of power</b>: DC collected taxes, kept order, judged disputes even from his own tax decisions", "<b>Bombay 1819:</b> same system by <b>Elphinstone</b> (follower of Munro's philosophy)", "Result: <b>Madras Torture Commission Report 1855</b>, oppression by <b>Mirasidars</b> revealed", w=30),
  bx('ye', "<b>Madras Torture Commission 1855, two homes:</b> handout puts it in police (4.3.2: atrocities of revenue officials after Daroga failed in Madras); class puts it in Ryotwari judiciary (DC with all powers + juniors, Mirasidars). Learn once: 1855, oppression exposed; use in either answer. <b>Munro 1814 vs 1820:</b> 1814 = judicial model replaced in Madras; 1820 = formal Ryotwari revenue rollout (Ch 16). Do not swap."),

