  t("<b>1833 impact</b>", "GG of India = <b>single central legislative authority</b>; laws equal for Indians + Britishers (one law for all)", "<b>Macaulay</b> Law Member; <b>Law Commission 1834</b>; codification substantially complete <b>1837</b>, full implementation after 1857: <b>CPC 1859, IPC 1860, CrPC 1861</b>", "<b>Subordinate judicial posts below District Judge opened to Indians</b> (follows Madras 1814)", "<b>Impact on common Indian:</b> justice <b>psychologically distant</b> (western, complex), <b>physically distant</b> (rural), <b>financially distant</b> (fees); served the educated + propertied; personal laws continued in marriage + inheritance; 'Western Edu 1835' (Ch 19): English-educated could use new courts", w=26),
  t("<b>Bentinck 28-35</b> (GG 1828-33; GG of India 1833-35)", "<b>Abolished divisional courts</b>: Cornwallis 86-93's <b>Provincial Courts of Appeal</b> (civil) + <b>Courts of Circuit</b> (criminal): <b>parking grounds for inefficient officers</b> (punishment postings), high pendency, <b>high State expenditure</b> = fiscal prudence; powers + pending cases to <b>District Judges</b>", "Concept: polity = L, E, J equal; reality: E top prestige, J dumping ground", "After him: civil = District Diwani Adalat + City Courts straight to SDA; criminal = Nizamat Adalat straight to SNA", "<b>1835</b> <b>Persian replaced</b>: vernaculars in lower courts, <b>English in higher</b> (<b>Act XXIX of 1837</b>); anxiety among <b>Muslim elites</b> (Persian = path to careers)", "<b>NWP courts:</b> own <b>SDA + SNA</b> in Northwest Provinces (Awadh portion annexed <b>1801</b>, full province status <b>1836</b>) so no travel to Bengal ('Distance')", w=32),
  bx('bl', "<b>Persian context (handout):</b> introduced under Delhi Sultanate in 13th century; boosted when <b>Humayun 30-40</b> accepted promoting Persian to win Safavid military support vs Suri Dynasty (1540-55); <b>Akbar 56-05</b> with finance minister Todar Mal made Persian compulsory for administrative records."),
