  t("<b>Aitchison Commission 1887</b> (Lecture 21)", "Appointed <b>1886</b> by <b>Dufferin 84-88</b>; report <b>1887</b>: drop 'Covenanted/Uncovenanted'; <b>three tiers: Imperial Civil Service (ICS), Provincial Civil Service (PCS), Subordinate Civil Service</b>", "Implemented <b>1892 by executive order under Lansdowne 88-94</b> (NOT Indian Councils Act 1892, Ch 28 Lord Cross Act, exam trap): <b>CCS became ICS, UCS became PCS</b>, <b>Statutory CS (1878) abolished</b> (partly by Moderate pressure)", "<b>PCS</b> = UCS senior posts + Statutory CS, recruited by exams + selection <b>in India</b>; <b>Subordinate</b> = UCS junior posts (clerks)", "Context: Moderate phase 1885-1905 'Pressure on Britain'; provincial service gets own commission only <b>GOI 1935</b>", w=28),
  t("<b>Islington Commission (1912)</b>", "Context: Swadeshi 1905-11, Delhi Conspiracy Case 1912, Ghadar 1913-15, Home Rule Leagues 1916-18, WW I 1914-19", "Set up <b>1912</b>, report <b>1917</b>: <b>25% Indians</b> in senior posts via <b>exam (DR)</b> + <b>promotion from PCS (promotees)</b>; <b>rejected simultaneous exam in India</b> (uneven standards)", "Teacher: <b>'CONTRADICTION'</b>: 25% promised yet refused the reform that would win it; real reason (handout): slow down Indianisation, fear more Indian candidates; star note: <b>first time reservation recommended</b> (1919 first implemented)", w=24),
