  sec("POLICE", 'b'),
  t("<b>Inherited system (pre-1781)</b>", "Mughal policing left untouched longest (sensitive)", "<b>Naib Nazim</b> (Deputy Subadar; Md Reza Khan) @ <b>suba</b> = overall head; <b>Faujdars</b> @ <b>district / rural Sarkars</b> ('Sarkar' here = sub-divisional unit); <b>Kotwals</b> @ <b>towns</b>; <b>Zamindars</b> in villages, <b>paid Village Watchmen (Chowkidars)</b> one per village from own resources", w=22),
  t("<b>Hastings 73-85's 1781 reforms</b>", "GBF 1770 raised crime; <b>Faujdars replaced by English Magistrates (DC/DM)</b> in rural districts; Zamindars kept police duty under DM", "<b>Problem:</b> <b>very few DMs</b>, poor supervision, Zamindars oppress freely. Chain: GG(Be) > DC/DM > Zamindars > Village Watchmen", w=22),
  t("<b>Daroga system of Cornwallis 86-93 (1793)</b> ('PS 1793 + Code 1793 = one package')", "<b>Ended Zamindars' police powers</b> (agrarian capitalists, not police)", "District divided into <b>thanas of 30 sq miles</b> (1 mile = 1.6 km: about 77 sq km); each under new <b>Daroga (Indian)</b> appointed + supervised by DM", "<b>English DM = absolute supreme head</b> of law and order in district; ultimate oversight in <b>GG + Council</b> (no IG or Naib Nazim between). Chain: <b>Darogas > DM > central govt</b>", w=26),
  tb(["Hat", "Role", "Mughal ancestor"], ["<b>DC (revenue)</b>", "Collects LR, manages govt land, land records, various taxes", "Diwani / Amalguzar function"], ["<b>DM (law and order)</b>", "Heads district criminal administration; coordinates with SP; peace, riots, executive orders e.g. <b>Section 144 CrPC</b>", "Nizamat / Faujdari function"]),
  bx('bl', "<b>DC and DM = usually one person</b> (as today). Cornwallis 86-93 separated the judicial function (DC/DM no longer judge); revenue + law and order stayed combined."),
  bx('ye', "<b>Faujdar = SP, or DM = heir of Faujdari?</b> Lecture 20: 'Faujdar = like SP at district'; Lecture 21: DM descends from Nizamat / Faujdari function. Answer: <b>the DM inherits the Faujdari function; the Faujdar was like today's SP.</b> Do not say the DM is the Faujdar."),
  t("<b>Daroga-Zamindar nexus (failure)</b>", "Zamindars <b>bribed Darogas</b>, kept <b>lathiyals</b>: main oppression of rural poor early 1800s; British blamed 'Indian corruption' not structure", "<b>1799 Wellesley 98-05 restored police powers to Zamindars</b> (admitted failure)", "<b>1802</b> Daroga system extended to <b>Madras</b>, later abolished; police powers to <b>DC's juniors</b> (revenue officials)", "<b>Atrocities exposed by Madras Torture Commission 1855</b> (see conflict above)", w=24),
  t("<b>Police Act 1861 and the Irish Constabulary model</b>", "After failure, <b>Irish Constabulary model</b>: centralised, hierarchical, quasi-military, effective in Ireland <b>since 1787</b>, for suppressing agitation as much as crime = <b>political control mechanism</b>", "<b>Road-test:</b> <b>Sindh 1843</b> (<b>Charles Napier</b>, Sindh Police right after conquest), <b>Punjab 1849</b>, <b>Bombay 1853</b>, <b>Madras 1859</b>", "<b>1st Police Commission 1860</b> set by <b>Canning 56-62</b> under <b>M.H. Court</b>: formalised what worked, borrowed the Sindh model", w=26),
  bx('ye', "<b>Trap:</b> Charles Napier did NOT head the 1860 commission (many guidebooks wrongly say so). Napier = blueprint (Sindh); <b>M.H. Court's</b> commission drew the national map."),
  t("<b>Police Act 1861</b>", "Passed <b>March 1861 by the GG's Council</b> (as restructured by Charter 1853), not the British Parliament; <b>Indian Councils Act 1861</b> came August 1861 (created Imperial Legislative Council, ILC): do not mix", "<b>Provincial police structure:</b> each province <b>own police</b> (own resources + HR; <b>specialist</b> ladder, not Zamindar or DC)", "<b>Operational chain:</b> <b>SI > SP > IG</b>; <b>political accountability</b> to civilian authority: <b>SP to DC/DM, IG to Governor / LG</b>", "Only an organisation chart: posts without a service: military officers or nominated Europeans, no cadre, no exam, no unified service (IPS not created yet)", "From <b>1857</b> a <b>'Police Raj'</b>: Indians excluded from senior posts; intelligence, political surveillance, 'ensure no repeat of 1857'", w=30),
  tb(["Post", "In charge of", "Reports to"], ["<b>Inspector General (IG)</b>", "Provincial police", "Governor / LG"], ["<b>Superintendent of Police (SP)</b>", "District police", "DC / DM"], ["<b>Sub-Inspector (SI)</b>", "Thana", "<b>SP</b> (not DC as earlier)"]),
  tb(["Year", "Formalisation into a cadre"], ["<b>1893</b>", "First open competitive exam for senior police posts, London; top candidates = probationary Assistant SPs under SoS"], ["<b>1902-03</b>", "<b>Curzon 99-05</b> set <b>2nd Police Commission under Sir Andrew Fraser</b> (report 1903): one unified all-India cadre, <b>Imperial Police (IP)</b> (informally Indian Police); from about 1905"], ["Fraser's package", "<b>Provincial Police Service (PPS)</b> with new rank <b>DySP</b> for Indians, always junior to British IP; <b>CID in every province</b> + <b>Department of Criminal Intelligence (1903)</b> = forerunner of <b>IB</b>; IP itself <b>closed to Indians</b>: Fraser did NOT recommend Indians (preserving racial superiority at top)"], ["<b>1920</b>", "Direct entry to IP opened to Indians (simultaneous exams England + India <b>from 1921</b>) after GOI Act 1919"], ["By <b>1931</b>", "Only <b>20% of SPs</b> Indian"], ["From <b>1939</b>", "More Indians posted as SP: British candidates recruited for WW II / WWII (1939-45)"], ["<b>1948</b>", "IP replaced by <b>Indian Police Service (IPS)</b> by Home Ministry resolution; statutory backing <b>All India Services Act 1951</b>"]),
  bx('pk', "<b>1861 built the structure, 1902-03 built the service, 1948-51 built the IPS.</b> Today's IPS = AIS under <b>Article 312</b>; State police under State governments inherit 1861 framework. Police exam in India began <b>1921</b>; ICS exam in India <b>1922</b> (board '* ICS exam in India: 1922')."),
